  "notes": [
    "Live REA stdio MCP over the main+DllBattle carrier (session outputs/rea-battle-6, analyses and byte reads); every instruction and literal word equals the original DllBattle.cro bytes, except literal 108a68e0 (Starf's stat table 108d2c3a), an ABS32 relocation whose original word and S+A value are checked. The five table bytes equal the original read-only segment bytes.",
    "Eight handlers have no Ghidra function (analyze_function refuses them; inspect_native_instruction reports their words undecodable); their listings come from ../battle_power/reproduction/decode_arm.py, which reproduces every supported REA-listed instruction, and a bx<cond> rule for the one form it refuses, which reproduces REA's listing of the reference word 108695c4 (bxeq lr).",
    "The five event-0x7c Figy uses return when work word 6 is zero and otherwise run the event-0x7b stub sequence inline; 108a7d34 and 108a6a50 are event-0x7b stubs; 108a5fc0 is Lansat's use.",
    "Static analysis plus host comparison; not a matching original build."
  ]
